# Line-ending policy.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set locally and this repository carried no
# `.gitattributes`, so every text file is rewritten to CRLF in the working tree
# on checkout. That is harmless for almost everything here: DC-1 normalises CRLF
# to LF before hashing, so every digest, seal, registry row and approval binding
# is immune to it by construction.
#
# It is NOT harmless for a generated artifact that is compared byte-for-byte.
# `params/generated/SEWCP-200.csv` is emitted with LF endings and no byte-order
# mark, and is imported directly by Fusion 360 at CAD package step 6.02. A
# stash/checkout round-trip rewrote it to CRLF and broke
# `python -m aief_params check`, which is how this file came to exist.
params/generated/*.csv text eol=lf
